From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: a soft reset clears the dupterm slots before the heap
 sweep.

The soft reset swept the heap, then wrote "MPY: soft reboot", and only then
did mp_init() clear the dupterm slots. A stream written in Python and
attached with os.dupterm() had already been freed when that message reached
its write() method, so the call ran on freed memory: on an ESP32-S3 it ended
in a LoadProhibited panic, or in an AttributeError from whatever object had
reused the memory, after which dupterm deactivated the slot. The slots are
now cleared before the sweep, as stm32 and rp2 effectively do by printing
the message first.
---
 ports/esp32/main.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ports/esp32/main.c b/ports/esp32/main.c
--- a/ports/esp32/main.c
+++ b/ports/esp32/main.c
@@ -216,6 +216,15 @@
     mp_usbd_deinit();
     #endif
 
+    #if MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM
+    // The sweep below frees every dupterm stream, but the slots are only
+    // cleared in mp_init(), after the "soft reboot" message has been written
+    // to them. Clear them first, or that write calls into freed memory.
+    for (size_t i = 0; i < MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM; ++i) {
+        MP_STATE_VM(dupterm_objs[i]) = MP_OBJ_NULL;
+    }
+    #endif
+
     gc_sweep_all();
 
     // Free any native code pointers that point to iRAM.
